B.cA=new A.W(983712,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.arh=new A.i0(B.cA,"When to add Dobutamine \u2014 research add-on","Add dobutamine 5\u201315 \u03bcg/kg/min when there is myocardial dysfunction (pulmonary oedema, gallop, EF < 40 %). Continue until warm shock resolves. Avoid dopamine \u2014 pure \u03b1-effect worsens venom-induced vasoconstriction.",null)
B.ari=new A.i0(B.cA,"Atropine + neostigmine for neurotoxicity","For krait/cobra neurotoxicity: Atropine 0.05 mg/kg + Neostigmine 0.04 mg/kg IV. Reassess at 30 min \u2014 if improved, repeat neostigmine 0.04 mg/kg with atropine 0.025 mg/kg every 30 min \xd7 5 doses, then 1\u20132 hourly.",null)
B.dU=new A.W(58236,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.arj=new A.i0(B.dU,"Severity assessment \u2014 research add-on","GINA 2023 criteria for acute severe asthma in children:\n\u2022 Talks in words / unable to complete sentences\n\u2022 Sits hunched forward, agitated\n\u2022 RR > 30/min, accessory muscle use\n\u2022 HR > 120/min\n\u2022 SpO\u2082 < 90 % on room air\n\u2022 PEF \u2264 50 % predicted/personal best",null)
B.O5=new A.W(58977,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.ark=new A.i0(B.O5,"How fast to drop BP","Aim to reduce SBP by 1/3\u02b3\u1d48 in the first 12 hours, a further 1/3\u02b3\u1d48 over the next 12 hours, and the final 1/3\u02b3\u1d48 over the next 24 hours (towards 90\u1d57\u02b0\u201395\u1d57\u02b0 centile). Faster drops risk watershed cerebral ischaemia and posterior reversible encephalopathy syndrome (PRES).",null)
B.arl=new A.i0(B.dU,"ASV reconstitution + dosing \u2014 research add-on","India: Polyvalent ASV covers Big Four (Cobra, Krait, Russell's viper, Saw-scaled viper). Reconstitute each vial in 10 mL sterile water; dilute total in 200\u2013250 mL NS. Infuse over 60 min. Children get the SAME dose as adults \u2014 venom load is the same. Repeat every 6 h until WBCT < 20 min and neurotoxicity reverses or stabilises.",null)
B.arm=new A.i0(B.dU,"Consider atropine + cricoid pressure","Atropine 0.02 mg/kg IV (min 0.1 mg, max 1 mg) for < 5 yr or any patient receiving succinylcholine. Hold cricoid pressure from loss of consciousness until ETT is confirmed.",null)
B.arn=new A.i0(B.dU,"Dialysable poison mnemonic \u2014 ISTUMBLE","I \u2014 Isopropanol, S \u2014 Salicylates, T \u2014 Theophylline, U \u2014 Uraemia, M \u2014 Methanol, B \u2014 Barbiturates (long-acting), L \u2014 Lithium, E \u2014 Ethylene glycol. Useful one-line memory aid for the dialysable poisons list.",null)
B.aro=new A.i0(B.dU,"Avoid SL nifedipine in <2 yr \u2014 research add-on",'Sublingual / "bite-and-swallow" nifedipine can cause precipitous BP drop and stroke in younger children. AAP 2017 BP guideline reserves it for children > 2 yr where IV access is delayed. Safer alternative in infants is oral isradipine 0.05\u20130.1 mg/kg.',null)
B.ly=new A.W(62223,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.arp=new A.i0(B.ly,"Activated charcoal \u2014 single dose protocol","1 g/kg PO/NG (max 50 g) within 1 hour of ingestion. Can be given later for sustained-release preparations or anticholinergics that delay gastric emptying. Multi-dose activated charcoal (0.5 g/kg q 4\u20136 h) for carbamazepine, phenobarbital, theophylline, dapsone, quinine.",null)
B.arq=new A.i0(B.dU,'"P or U" = airway is at risk',"Any AVPU level worse than V (i.e., P or U) means the patient cannot reliably protect their airway. Position laterally, suction, and prepare for intubation. Recheck every 5\u201310 minutes during transport.",null)
B.arr=new A.i0(B.dU,"Confirming ETT placement (research add-on)","Gold standard: continuous waveform capnography (ETCO\u2082 trace). Other confirmations: bilateral chest rise, equal air entry, no epigastric sounds, condensation in tube, SpO\u2082 rising. CXR after stabilisation for tip position (target T2\u2013T3 in children, mid-trachea).",null)
B.ars=new A.i0(B.dU,"WBCT-20 \u2014 research add-on","Whole-blood clotting time at 20 minutes is the bedside test for viper envenomation. Place 1\u20132 mL of fresh blood in a clean, dry test tube. Leave undisturbed 20 min. If still liquid \u2192 coagulopathy \u2192 ASV indicated. Repeat 6-hourly until normal.",null)
B.art=new A.i0(B.dU,"GCS thresholds \u2014 research add-on","\u2022 13\u201315 = mild head injury\n\u2022 9\u201312 = moderate head injury\n\u2022 \u2264 8 = severe head injury \u2192 secure airway (ETT) and admit to ICU.\n\nAlways document the components separately (E/M/V), not just the total \u2014 a GCS 8 made up of E1\xb7M5\xb7V2 is very different from E2\xb7M2\xb7V4.",null)
B.aru=new A.i0(B.dU,"Therapy phases (research add-on)","0\u20135 min: Stabilisation phase \u2014 adrenaline, atropine, volume.\n5\u201320 min: Initial therapy phase \u2014 start vasoactive infusion (dopamine / adrenaline).\n20\u201340 min: Second therapy phase \u2014 escalate to noradrenaline + inotropic support.\n40\u201360 min: Third therapy phase \u2014 milrinone, levosimendan, vasopressin; consider HFO/ECMO referral.",null)
B.arv=new A.i0(B.dU,"Rough AVPU \u2194 GCS mapping (research add-on)","A \u2014 GCS 14\u201315 (alert, no deficit)\nV \u2014 GCS 12\u201313 (eye opening to voice)\nP \u2014 GCS 8 (responds only to pain \u2014 protect airway, often intubation threshold)\nU \u2014 GCS \u2264 6 (no response \u2014 definitely intubate)",null)
B.arw=new A.i0(B.dU,"Prazosin \u2014 research add-on","Prazosin is a selective post-synaptic \u03b11-blocker. It reverses the autonomic storm of Mesobuthus tamulus (Indian Red Scorpion) venom. Pune protocol (Bawaskar): 30 \u03bcg/kg PO repeat q 3 h \xd7 3 doses, then q 6 h until warm peripheries. First dose hypotension is rare in scorpion sting because the patient is already vasoconstricted.",null)
B.arx=new A.i0(B.ly,"Sodium nitroprusside cyanide caution","Maximum recommended dose 10 mCg/kg/min for \u2264 10 min; for longer use, stay \u2264 4 mCg/kg/min. Monitor lactate, mixed venous saturation and acid-base. Co-infuse sodium thiosulphate in renal failure or prolonged use to scavenge cyanide.",null)
B.ary=new A.i0(B.dU,"Dry bite \u2014 research add-on",'20\u201350 % of venomous snake bites are "dry bites" with no envenomation. Observe for at least 24 hours regardless \u2014 symptoms (esp. neurological from kraits) can be delayed by 6\u201312 hours. Always recheck WBCT-20 at 6 h.',null)
B.arz=new A.i0(B.ly,"Pitfalls \u2014 research add-on",'\u2022 Intubated patient: V is scored "1T" (chart it explicitly).\n\u2022 Periorbital oedema can prevent eye opening \u2014 chart "1C".\n\u2022 Sedation, hypoglycaemia and hypoxia all artificially lower GCS \u2014 correct first, reassess.',null)
B.arA=new A.i0(B.cA,"When to intubate \u2014 research add-on","Indications: deteriorating mental status, exhaustion, rising pCO\u2082 > 50 mmHg with worsening acidosis, refractory hypoxaemia. Use ketamine 1\u20132 mg/kg + rocuronium 1 mg/kg as RSI. Avoid morphine (histamine release). Permissive hypercapnia + low rate (8\u201312) + long expiratory time (I:E 1:3 to 1:5) to avoid breath stacking.",null)
B.arB=new A.i0(B.dU,"IV magnesium \u2014 preferred escalation","After 1 h of standard therapy with no improvement, IV MgSO\u2084 40\u201350 mg/kg (max 2 g) over 20 min is the first escalation. Watch BP \u2014 magnesium is a vasodilator. Hypotension settles with fluid bolus.",null)
B.arC=new A.i0(B.dU,"Pitfalls (research add-on)","\u2022 Propofol infusion syndrome \u2014 risk > 4 mg/kg/hr beyond 48 h. Watch for metabolic acidosis, rhabdomyolysis, cardiac failure.\n\u2022 Ketamine \u2014 increases salivary secretions; pre-treat with glycopyrrolate.\n\u2022 Vecuronium / rocuronium \u2014 accumulate in renal/liver failure; prefer atracurium / cisatracurium (Hofmann elimination \u2014 degraded by plasma esterase).\n\u2022 Midazolam \u2014 prolonged sedation, immunosuppression; intubate if used following benzodiazepines.",null)
B.arD=new A.lD("Acute Severe Asthma card. Research add-ons draw on the GINA Global Strategy for Asthma Management 2023, BTS/SIGN British Asthma Guideline 2019 and the AAP Section on Pulmonology consensus. For use by qualified clinicians only \u2014 verify against the patient's clinical context and your local protocol before administering.",null)
B.arE=new A.lD("ELECTROLYTE CORRECTIONS card. Every value transcribed verbatim. Calculator chips link to the matching tools inside this app. For use by qualified clinicians only.",null)
B.arF=new A.lD("Hypertensive Emergency flowchart + Antihypertensive Drugs tables. Research add-ons draw on the AAP Clinical Practice Guideline for Screening and Management of High Blood Pressure in Children and Adolescents (2017) and the ESH 2022 paediatric hypertension consensus. For use by qualified clinicians only.",null)
B.arG=new A.lD("Glasgow Coma Scale Score card. Smart score interactivity + thresholds + pitfalls drawn from Teasdale & Jennett (Lancet 1974) and APLS 6th edition. For use by qualified clinicians only.",null)
B.arH=new A.lD("Glasgow Coma Scale Score reference page. For use by qualified clinicians only.",null)
B.arI=new A.lD("Snake Envenomation & Management card. Research add-ons draw on WHO SE-Asia Regional Snakebite Guidelines (2016) and the ICMR Indian Snakebite Management Protocol. For use by qualified clinicians only \u2014 verify against local antivenom availability and the patient's clinical context before administration.",null)
B.arJ=new A.lD("Rapid Sequence Intubation (Flow & Medications Used) card. Research add-ons drawn from APLS 6th edition and the PALS RSI consensus. For use by qualified clinicians only.",null)
B.arK=new A.lD("Medications Used For Seizures Control. Status ladder add-on per Status Epilepticus Treatment Guideline (Glauser et al., Neurol Clin Pract 2016) and ESETT trial. For use by qualified clinicians only.",null)
B.arL=new A.lD('Level of Consciousness Assessment "AVPU" card. Mapping + airway pearls drawn from APLS 6th edition (Advanced Paediatric Life Support) and the BMJ Best Practice paediatric trauma pathway. For use by qualified clinicians only.',null)
